course: dictionary
lesson: 4972
title: Incomplete
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word often gives a clue. In- often means not, so incomplete means not complete: not finished, or with some parts missing.
explain: «Because it was raining.» tells you a reason, but it does not say what happened. It is an incomplete sentence because a main part is missing. Ask yourself: does it make full sense on its own?
explain: The same idea works in maths and science. A table with blank boxes is incomplete, and so is a set of science data with gaps in it. Look for what is missing.
fact: Incomplete means not finished or with some parts missing.
fact: «Incomplete» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in incomplete homework.
fact: An incomplete sentence is missing a main part, so it does not make full sense on its own.
fact: An incomplete maths table has missing numbers, and incomplete data has gaps in it.
fact: The opposite of incomplete is complete.
exercise: Why is «Because it was raining.» an incomplete sentence? | It is a question | *It is missing a main part, so it does not make full sense alone | It is too long
exercise: Maya's times table has blank boxes. What word describes the table? | Perfect | Correct | *Incomplete | Complete
exercise: Find the adjective in: «Ravi handed in his incomplete homework.» | homework | *incomplete | handed | his
test: Which word means the opposite of incomplete? | Partial | Broken | *Complete | Missing
test: «The science data was incomplete, with gaps in the results.» What does incomplete mean here? | Written in pencil | Finished and perfect | *Not finished, with parts missing | Very large
exam: What does incomplete mean? | Very old | *Not finished or with some parts missing | Full of light | Happy and calm
